<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cape Town</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1652">1652</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cape Town is a port city on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/table-bay">Table Bay</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>. It was founded in 1652 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-van-riebeeck">Jan van Riebeeck</a> as a supply station of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> and grew into the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a>, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and then British rule. Since 1910 it has been the legislative capital of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cape-town.jpg" alt="Cape Town" width="320" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Der Berzerker from Washington, DC, USA · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Camps_bay_(53460319478)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
